# Local-only, never published: internal changelog, chip/EDA/AIG/GCU notes,
# NCGD/PinEKF source, simulated peer-review transcripts, scratch.
*.local.md
*.local.json
_local/
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# What is deliberately NOT ignored, and why
# ----------------------------------------
# An earlier revision of this file excluded the official manifest and the whole
# of results/cryptobench_official/. That made the headline comparison
# unauditable from a clone: a reader could see the frozen bootstrap but not the
# per-structure telemetry it was computed from, and could not recompute either.
# The manifests, labels, telemetry, per-structure predictions and raw P2Rank
# output are all small (about 18 MB together) and are committed for that reason.
# Only inputs that are reproducible byte-for-byte from a pinned hash, and
# derived caches that are reproducible from those inputs, are excluded below.

# Structure coordinates: 185 MB, materialized from RCSB and OSF and verified
# against the SHA-256 pins already committed in the manifests.
#   tools/fetch_official_data.py
data/cryptobench_apo/_osf/
data/cryptobench_apo/official_receptors/
data/cryptobench_apo/train_receptors/

# Derived feature caches: ~700 MB, rebuilt from the receptors above.
#   tools/build_cascade_cache.py, tools/build_expanded_cache.py
data/cryptobench_apo/_*.npz
data/cryptobench_apo/_*.npy
# Sidecar recording what a derived cache was built from, so a stale one is
# rebuilt rather than trusted. tools/digit_cache.py writes it beside the .npy.
data/cryptobench_apo/_*.json
data/cryptobench_apo/_scratch/
# Holo depositions fetched to recover the labelling rule. 300 MB of
# public PDB files, refetchable by name from the committed sample seed.
data/cryptobench_apo/_holo/
# Depositions fetched to label the external set. 1.6 GB of public PDB
# and mmCIF files, refetchable by name from the committed manifest.
data/external/_structures/
# EMDB density volumes, tens to hundreds of MB each, refetchable by accession
# from the figure provenance. Ignored before the first one finished downloading:
# a 292 MB set of third-party binaries reached this repository's history once and
# is still in it, and the rule that would have stopped it is this one.
data/external/_emdb/
# The pinned P2Rank distribution: 292 MB of third-party binaries, one file
# over GitHub's limit. What makes the baseline auditable is the archived CSVs,
# the recorded command, version banner and digests, all of which are tracked.
# Reinstall the exact release with bin/install-p2rank.sh.
.tools/

# The pLM-NN baseline's weights, read out of the SavedModel published on OSF and
# reproducible byte-for-byte from the digests recorded beside them.
#   tools/export_plmnn_weights.py
results/baselines/PLMNN_WEIGHTS.npz
results/baselines/_plmnn_checkpoint.jsonl
# The same resumable scratch for the two later encoder passes: the training-fold
# fit-set audit and the Set B/C read. Both are summarised completely by the
# artifacts they produce, and a half-finished pass is meaningful only to the
# process that was running it.
results/baselines/_plmnn_train_checkpoint.jsonl
results/baselines/_plmnn_setbc_checkpoint.jsonl
results/baselines/_plmnn_setn_checkpoint.jsonl

# PocketMiner's own repository, sparse-checked-out at the commit
# tools/pocketminer_run.py pins, and the interpreter it needs. 183 MB of weights,
# source and their own labelled apo structures, plus a 1.5 GB TensorFlow that
# cannot share an environment with the frozen pipeline because it pins an older
# numpy. Both are rebuilt by the recipe in the tool's docstring; the two weight
# files are verified by SHA-256 on every run.
third_party/pocketminer/
.venv-pocketminer/

# P2Rank's per-residue scores on the 770 training receptors: an intermediate
# behind P2RANK_TRAIN_OPERATING_POINT.json, which records its sha256 and the
# decision it supports. Rebuilt by tools/p2rank_train_operating_point.py, which
# needs the JVM exactly as the committed P2Rank summaries already do.
results/architecture_sweep/_p2rank_train_residues.npz

# Resumable-run scratch, meaningful only to an interrupted process.
results/**/_scoring_checkpoint.jsonl

# Rust build artefacts for the optional native kernels
native/geoaudit_kernels/target/

# LaTeX build artefacts
paper/*.pdf
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.xdv

# PocketMiner per-residue scores on the 770 training receptors: the intermediate
# behind POCKETMINER_TRAIN_OPERATING_POINT.json, which records its sha256 and the
# threshold it supports. Rebuilt by tools/pocketminer_run.py --predict --train.
data/baselines/pocketminer_train/
results/baselines/POCKETMINER_TRAIN_SCORES.json

data/external/_setb_probe_em_*.json
data/cryptobench_apo/_aniso_cache_train.npz

# Scratch logs from supervised long runs; nothing here is evidence.
_tmp/

# Per-split checkpoints of long sweeps; the artifact is the evidence, not these.
results/**/*.splits.jsonl

# Set N / Set B-C P2Rank intermediates (rewritten while scoring)
results/external/setn_p2rank_raw/
results/external/setbc_p2rank_raw/
# Set N geometry_field sequential resume
results/baselines/_geometry_setn_checkpoint.jsonl
data/msa_cache/

# 956 deposited PDB archives, 190 MB, each a byte-identical copy of a public
# RCSB download. DEPOSITED_ENTRY_MANIFEST.json pins every one by sha256 and
# tools/fetch_deposited_entries.py re-fetches them, so the input is pinned
# without the bytes riding in the repository.
data/deposited_entries/*.gz
